Assignment Goals.
1. Compare word frequencies between two works of a single author.
2. Compare word frequencies between works of two authors.
3. Are there some words preferred by one author but used less frequently by another author?

In order to reach this goal, I think a good author to choose from would be William Shakespeare. 
He has a wide vocabulary and can be somewhat inconsistent with his more flexible grammar, which
would make it interesting to see which patterns stick across his works. I would suggest two of his
most famous works, Romeo and Juliet and Hamlet.

For comparing word frequencies between works of two different authors, I think interesting ones to 
compare would be Shakespeare and Edgar Allan Poe. Poe's works preceded Shakespeare's by about 200 years
which would make it interesting to see how writing style and grammatical convention were further
developed during that time. Works by both authors are publicly accessible and can be found online.
